  m_text: Scientists use the Mohs Scale (1 to 10) to measure the hardness of minerals.
    Hardness is determined by what can scratch a mineral. Is the mineral soft enough
    to be scratched by a fingernail, or is it so hard that only a diamond can scratch
    it? The higher the number is, the harder the mineral.
